  note = {PageMem = a deterministic structured-DOM representation (4-level WebsiteMem $\to$ PageMem $\to$ PageSection (DOM subtree + LLM one-sentence summary) $\to$ Element), with offline-exploration persistent memory, a multi-stage select-then-summarize observation pipeline (selective attention), and compound-action workflows; numbered-list-index action, not tool-calling. Backbone GLM-4-32B-0414, no fine-tune; its VisualWebArena vision model is Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct (= our B1). WebArena 56.3\% (open-agent SOTA, +7.9 over Mobile-Agent-v3.5); VWA 48.7\%; harness-isolation GLM-4-32B 19.4\% (minimal GenericAgent) $\to$ 58.8\% (WebChallenger), a +39.4pt ``architecture not scale'' claim. Cited in our paper \S 6.8 as the fixed-representation contrast pole: WebChallenger commits every page to a SINGLE structured DOM view, whereas we route per task among DOM/SoM/Vision/phantom; its within-page section selection is intra-representation attention, not cross-mode routing. Its harness-isolation design (same model, minimal-vs-rich harness) is a clean template for reporting a representation contribution net of model scale. CAVEAT: NOT a baseline --- different controller (GLM-4-32B vs our Qwen/Gemma), full VWA-910 with an offline exploration phase, and PageMem bundles memory+workflows so its SR is not attributable to representation alone; SR incomparable to ours. Added 2026-06-15 from cron\_digest\_2026-06-12 triage, arXiv id API-verified.}
